{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers","id":105380,"title":"Filing off the serial numbers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-03T22:21:00-07:00","id":105380,"title":"Filing off the serial numbers?","content":"Has anyone done any work on doing away with the faux-Egyptian trappings inherent in the mechanics of <i>Mummy: the Curse</i>? What about doing away with the Iremite mythology?<br /> <br /> (Note: I'm not trying to stir up trouble, just looking for a more generic M:tC in-line with the vaguer nWoD of the other gamelines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T22:23:53-07:00","id":105381,"title":"","content":"So do you mean like make the Nameless Empire more nebulous so it could be like Atlantis, or Asgard, or some other mythic place of your choice? That sounds doable. After all the Shan'iatu might have even come from such a place themselves before Irem.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with changing things up for a Chronicle, you're not hurting anyone and it can be fun to make an alternate setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T22:39:34-07:00","id":105384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers?p=105381#post105381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you mean like make the Nameless Empire more nebulous so it could be like Atlantis, or Asgard, or some other mythic place of your choice? That sounds doable. After all the Shan'iatu might have even come from such a place themselves before Irem.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with changing things up for a Chronicle, you're not hurting anyone and it can be fun to make an alternate setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. The Atlantis of <i>Mage: the Awakening</i> is a very nebulous thing, and may not have existed as envisioned by the modern Awakened (the Dark Era for Mage doesn't even have the unified Atlantis myth yet); there's an entire book about possibilities for it all over the globe. I'd love to see the Nameless Empire given a similar treatment, with the Guilds, Decrees, Pillars, Judges, etc taken in a more generic direction, so as to allow Mummies from across the world without the Egyptian trappings or specific folklore.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T23:42:02-07:00","id":105410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers?p=105384#post105384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. The Atlantis of <i>Mage: the Awakening</i> is a very nebulous thing, and may not have existed as envisioned by the modern Awakened (the Dark Era for Mage doesn't even have the unified Atlantis myth yet); there's an entire book about possibilities for it all over the globe. I'd love to see the Nameless Empire given a similar treatment, with the Guilds, Decrees, Pillars, Judges, etc taken in a more generic direction, so as to allow Mummies from across the world without the Egyptian trappings or specific folklore.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem with that statement is that mummy is so tied to the Nameless Empire that attempting to file it off will risk making it nonsensical. After all, you have to ask where did mummies come from and the whole thing with Memory which if raised high enough simply reveals the entire nature of the setting to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T23:51:04-07:00","id":105415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers?p=105410#post105410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main problem with that statement is that mummy is so tied to the Nameless Empire that attempting to file it off will risk making it nonsensical. After all, you have to ask where did mummies come from and the whole thing with Memory which if raised high enough simply reveals the entire nature of the setting to the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's point, its a feature not a bug of this whole proposal. Its fun to come up with different reasons for things.<br /> <br /> Mind I do enjoy the Irem schtoof, I am agreeing though that it could be fun to must make up everything from the ground up for another chronicle. For instance I was suggesting what about having all the Shan'iatu be Sin Eaters, I'm not saying its the default setting, but it would be fun to make things with that conceit in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:58:57-07:00","id":105505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/105380-filing-off-the-serial-numbers?p=105384#post105384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(the Dark Era for Mage doesn't even have the unified Atlantis myth yet)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...I know why you're saying it like that, but on the other hand <i>Mage</i>'s Dark Era is sort of the reason why the Atlantis myth is so prevalent. It's nitpicky, but it's like saying a plant's seed isn't a plant itself. Like, not yet but it's got all the trappings for the eventuality of the situation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, like someone said above me said, I suppose the Nameless Empire isn't 'essential' but you do need to have something for Mummies to remember. Here's a few pieces of the puzzle to consider: 1) morally ambiguous sorcerers that mummified you to begin with 2) even more morally ambiguous demon-gods to whom you are eternally bound to serve 3) relics are very tied to the Guilds, so if you change the Guilds consider how that affects the nature of relics 4) it should -probably- be pseudo-historical and 'exist in this version of the timeline' (unlike <i>Mage</i>'s Atlantis) because this is the game where you get to play Indiana Jones.<br /> <br /> With that all said, the Nameless Empire's specifics aren't much more than the things I just mentioned. It's pretty vague on how things worked exactly anyway, so anything you want to say would probably fly. The 'problem' with a pseudo-historical culture is that it needs to take place somewhere, and Egypt is as good as any. But sure, it's plausible to be like, &quot;Actually my Irem wasn't on the Nile; it was in China.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's indulge a fantasy of mine, and we can imagine that the Nameless Empire predates Michael Moorcock's Melnibon\u00e8 and the Arisen watched that empire come and go, and it also watched Robert E. Howard's Thurian and Atlantean ages go by as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T08:17:24-07:00","id":105581,"title":"","content":"The problem with filing off Egypt is that, no matter what you do with the Nameless Empire thing... Its always going to have all Mummies coming from some ancient civilization. Most likely, some generic civilization still heavily influenced by western culture - good luck with having, say, Aztec or Chinese mummies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, what I would do if I had to do a Mummy minus Nameless Empire thing? Congrats, we are now playing Zombies!<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing about zombies is that, for the most part, they are like lesser versions of the big games. Flesh eating plague-bearing zombies? Vampires. Frankenstein-esk scientific zombies? Promethean. Zombies animated by a ghost or eldritch spirit, aka revenants? Geist. Zombies who were created by voodoo, or even some other magic that's known for something hinting at necromancy or raising the dead, such as, oh, the Egyptian Book of the Dead stuff? Mummy.<br /> <br /> So, Mummy, stripped of its origins as a &quot;we all come from this ancient civilization,&quot; would be a game about playing zombies resurrected by magic. Type V zombies are generally seen as slaves to some kind of necromancer or other thing - while that has a lot in common with vampire / sire relations, and prommie / creator relations, those games actually rarely touch on their actual Creators as a long term thing. So, Mummies enslaved to their creators (the judges) really should stay, but be forced into something much more generic and less mono-cultured.<br /> <br /> <br /> The game seems to revolve around recovering relics for your master, taking over the world for your master, and preparing for the ancient city to arise once more (and take over the world). Lots of preparing for your evil-necromancer-master coming back and taking over. Well, most evil necromancers seem to want to have giant necropolises they rule, so that can stay. We just don't need to call it &quot;the Nameless Empire.&quot; We don't need Relics to be ancient relics of a nameless egyptian place. They can be more modern, and devised by these various necromancers.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point, we basically come down to &quot;what can we do to make the necromancers (/judges) less Egyptian.&quot; To file that off, I'd say to make Duat to be a generic place of necromancy. Someone might stumble onto it, now and again. They tap into the &quot;Ancient Spirits of Evil&quot; from there, learn to make more Mummies. And they kill bunches of people, ascend to Duat as a godling judge, and then guide their servants to prepare a way back for them. This could be finding relics made by other necromancers. Preparing rituals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like the God Machine angels, Mummies are trusted servants of a godly being. Unlike a Demon game, Mummies are still servants, and &quot;falling&quot; from their service is a near-end-game situation. Still, that means that Memory should still play a major part, as necromancer-made zombies tend to be under mind control to serve. Memory is a measure of their free will against the necromancer-gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not familiar enough with the powers without referencing the book, but I think most of them can remain as is. Zombies are still servants of a god-wanna-be. Cults can be remain, but I'd personally like to make some cultists have a stronger, direct like to their necromancer-god-king person. That way, when they revive ya, they're effectively an agent of your boss. Maybe not, since this way it leaves it more open to abuse by wanna be cult masters too. Decisions, decisions.... Anyways, cults and powers I don't think are necessarily Egyptian in flavor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That leaves the guilds. And I'm not sold on guilds even with the standard game. So, its &quot;what I did for master when alive&quot; and part philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-04-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}